+
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# Design analysis for combo D4/3 + D13/2
+#
+# combo_design:
+#   a) concrete_behavior_trace:
+#     - Base geometry keeps the original funnel/U family, but the former mouth is capped with wall pixels.
+#       This removes the original "visible opening tells the direction" cue.
+#     - A single trigger marker replaces one wall pixel on the opposite closed bridge. Its color is the fill
+#       color, and it is the only non-bg non-wall pixel that touches the wall.
+#     - A separate 2-pixel external marker sits outside the capped side with a one-cell bg gap. The nearer
+#       pixel is the tail and the farther one is the head, so the pair points along the radiate axis.
+#     - Small trace:
+#       old:
+#         1. detect interior fill blob
+#         2. infer radiate direction from the wall's two open endpoints
+#         3. flood interior from the blob, then radiate out of the mouth
+#       combo:
+#         1. detect the wall-touching singleton trigger marker and treat it as wall-colored geometry
+#         2. decode the external 2-pixel arrow to choose which side is the virtual opening
+#         3. remove only the capped mouth cells between the arrow-selected endpoints
+#         4. start BFS from the trigger's inner neighbor in the arrow direction
+#         5. flood the interior, pass through the virtual mouth, and keep the original slanted boundary rays
+#       difference:
+#         旧逻辑依赖“内部 seed + 几何开口”；融合后改成“边框触发 + 外部箭头选开口侧”。
+#   b) complexity_calibration:
+#     - Trigger marker is exactly one wall-touching pixel, so it is visually distinct from the external arrow.
+#     - Direction marker has only 4 possible cardinal directions and always uses exactly 2 pixels, keeping
+#       the new freedom small and repeated across examples.
+#     - The wall family, obstacle shadows, and ray slopes remain from the original task, so the puzzle still
+#       reads as a modified b9e38dc0 rather than a new unrelated task.
+#   c) hidden_assumption_audit:
+#     - Original `fill_pos` was assumed to be passable interior cells. That fails because the fill-colored
+#       trigger now lies on the wall, so the solver must derive an interior start cell from the trigger.
+#     - Original endpoint detection assumed a true open mouth. That fails after capping, so the solver must
+#       first decode the external arrow, then virtually remove only the selected cap cells.
+#     - Original obstacle detection treated every non-bg non-fill non-wall pixel as a blocker. That would
+#       wrongly include the external arrow, so marker cells must be excluded from shadow casting.
+#     - Original "closest non-wall color to wall" still works only if the trigger is the wall-adjacent color
+#       and obstacles / arrow stay farther away; the generator explicitly enforces that spacing.
+#   d) placement_legality:
+#     - The capped side is chosen from the original mouth and stays within the original open-end margin, so
+#       the 2-pixel arrow with a one-cell gap fits inside the grid.
+#     - The trigger marker is placed only on the closed bridge at positions whose arrow-facing 4-neighbor is
+#       an interior cell, guaranteeing a valid BFS start candidate.
+#     - Obstacles are placed only on background cells, far from the wall and both marker types, so they do
+#       not overlap or visually merge with either marker.
+#   e) observability:
+#     - Across examples, humans see two distinct cues: a singleton wall-attached trigger and a detached
+#       2-pixel arrow. The output then expands from the trigger color and exits on the arrow side.
+#     - Because the mouth is visibly capped, the arrow is the only explicit directional token in the input.
+#   f) cleanliness:
+#     - The trigger stays on the wall; the arrow stays outside the wall with a bg gap; obstacles stay sparse
+#       and separated. No region carries more than one semantic layer.
+#   g) inferability_of_changes:
+#     - No hidden color remapping is introduced. The trigger's own color becomes the filled region, while the
+#       arrow is identified by shape and placement rather than by any numeric color ordering.
+#   post_change_solver_assumptions_and_generator_guarantees:
+#     - exactly one wall-touching non-bg non-wall pixel exists -> generator makes the trigger unique
+#     - exactly one 2-pixel cardinal external marker with unequal wall distances exists -> generator makes
