+
+def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
+    """
+    Fill a sealed funnel from a border trigger and radiate through the side named by an external arrow.
+
+    Input structure:
+    - bg is the most common color. The dominant non-bg color is a capped funnel/U wall whose former mouth is
+      now sealed by wall pixels.
+    - One singleton marker of the fill color is embedded on the opposite border of the wall, while a detached
+      2-pixel arrow marker sits outside the capped side. Other sparse non-bg pixels are obstacles.
+
+    Rule:
+    - Treat the wall-touching singleton as a trigger, recover the wall by folding that pixel back into the
+      border, and use the external arrow to decide which capped side becomes the virtual opening.
+    - Start the flood from the trigger's inner neighbor, fill the interior with the trigger color, pass
+      through the virtual mouth, and keep obstacle shadows along the arrow-selected radiate direction.
